{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5917,
  "title": "Keep the carousel still when arrow keys are pressed on a button or link inside a card",
  "body": "> <kbd>LEFT</kbd>/<kbd>RIGHT</kbd> on a button inside a carousel card scroll the carousel, then it scrolls back.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed <kbd>LEFT</kbd>/<kbd>RIGHT</kbd> on a button inside a carousel card scrolling the carousel, in PR [#5917](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5917), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nOn a button inside a card, the browser scrolled the carousel by 40 pixels and react-film centered the card again half a second later; holding the key scrolled the focused button out of view. <kbd>LEFT</kbd>/<kbd>RIGHT</kbd> now do nothing on buttons, links, and checkboxes inside a card.\n\n## Design\n\n- An allow-list of controls whose only native arrow action is scrolling (buttons, links, checkboxes, `role=\"button\"`, `role=\"link\"`), not a deny-list of inputs, so text inputs, radio buttons, selects, dates, media, and focusable scroll regions keep their native arrow keys.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `CarouselFilmStrip.js`: prevent the default of <kbd>LEFT</kbd>/<kbd>RIGHT</kbd> on those controls inside a card\n- `carousel/navigation.arrowKeys.button.html`: new test, snapshots 3–5 and 8–9, a hero card button and an Adaptive Card container with Action.OpenUrl (`role=\"link\"`) keep focus and the carousel does not scroll\n- `carousel/navigation.arrowKeys.formControls.html`: <kbd>RIGHT</kbd> on buttons no longer waits for a scroll; snapshots 4–7: <kbd>TAB</kbd> centers the hero card (#5926), then <kbd>LEFT</kbd>/<kbd>RIGHT</kbd> on its button keep it still\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n\n",
